# Bootstrap scripts are fetched straight from raw.githubusercontent.com, which serves the
# blob exactly as stored -- the checkout-side `eol` conversion never applies there.
#
# cmd.exe can mis-locate `goto`/`call :label` targets in LF-only batch files (a known,
# offset-dependent quirk; our current install.cmd parsed fine both ways when tested on
# 2026-10-04, so this is preventive). Storing install.cmd with CRLF in the blob itself
# removes the risk for every future edit: `-text` turns off line-ending normalization
# for it (the file is committed with CRLF).
*.cmd -text
# POSIX shell scripts must stay LF even in Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true would
# otherwise give `set -eu\r` and a broken shebang when run locally from Git Bash/WSL).
*.sh text eol=lf
